What was changed:

- macOS only. The Windows and Linux branches, the SQLite store (and with
  it switching Antigravity.app older than 2.0), the instance management,
  the WebSocket server, wake-up and the other platforms are not included.
- One OAuth client, read from a local oauth-client.json instead of
  constants in the source.
- Tokens are kept in the app's own macOS Keychain items instead of
  AES-encrypted files with their key beside them.
- A thread and blocking HTTP instead of async tasks and Tauri events; typed
  errors that keep no response body, token or secret; nothing about a login
  or a token is logged.
- Quota reads: no environment overrides, no autopush host, no onboardUser,
  no subscription tier or credit parsing (only the GCP ToS mark is read);
  loadCodeAssist only while a token lacks a project or the GCP ToS mark,
  and an answer without the mark is kept as no GCP ToS; a 429 or 5xx is
  not retried at once but waits longer before the next read; a quota
  summary that does not come back keeps the last full reading instead of
  caching one without it; the cache lives in the app's own folder.
- The pages the browser sees are translated to Vietnamese, error messages to
  English.
- Antigravity.app is quit with osascript and opened with open -b instead of
  closed by its process; it is never killed. The switch is checked with
  quota-axi afterwards, logged in the app's own folder, and watched for six
  hours for a running app writing its old login back.

A later milestone that adapts more of Cockpit Tools adds its parts to
